 on  many signs and doors this text signature  everywhere which says builders on  bolson's personal work hammer and even  your sledgehammer you've been carrying  around this entire time did you know  that different races have different run  speeds this clip shows a gerudo and a  goron running for cover from the rain  but if the gerudo is behind the goron  she's stuck behind him because he's  running too slow but if she's in front  of the goron their distance becomes  larger and larger because she can run  faster something nintendo didn't have to  think about but they did anyways  have you ever been in a situation where  you threw a weapon or shot a sword beam  and thought am i just bad or am i  missing these shots well there's a very  subtle bug that nintendo didn't fix when  you have the magnesis rune selected for  some reason anything thrown swings to  the upper right so no it's not just you  some players know that when it rains  some areas form large puddles this is  created by a very simple but effective  mechanic which is simple water asset  called field object puddle slowly moves  up to clip through the ground to  simulate a growing puddle then slowly  goes back down to simulate evaporating  water simple but genius  there are several special shield  modifiers you can pick up along your  journey such as guard up and durability  up sure these are useful but there's one  secret modifier in the game's code that  nintendo never released the surf up  modifier this would have given any  shield the surfing ability better than  the shield of mine's eye but slightly  worse than the ancient shield it's  unknown why this was removed but i wish  it was left in the game during the  development of breath of the wild there  were multiple types of liquid terrain  from basic water lava mud ice water  spring water and more but there's one  type that didn't make the final cut  poison water this had similar properties  to standard water but with the obvious  factor that it would n